msgid ""
"When Read the Docs builds your project, it sets the :envvar:`READTHEDOCS` "
"environment variable to the string ``'True'``. So within your Sphinx "
":file:`conf.py` file, you can vary the behavior based on this. For example:"
msgstr ""
"当 Read the Docs 构建你的项目时，它会把 :envvar:`READTHEDOCS` 环境变量设置为字符串 ``'True'`` "
"。因此，在你的 Sphinx :file:`conf.py` 文件中，你可以据此改变行为。例如："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:155
msgid ""
"The :envvar:`READTHEDOCS` variable is also available in the Sphinx build "
"environment, and will be set to ``True`` when building on Read the Docs:"
msgstr ""
":envvar:`READTHEDOCS` 变量在 Sphinx 构建环境中同样可用，在 Read the Docs 上构建时它会被设为 "
"``True`` ："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:167
msgid "I want comments in my docs"
msgstr "我想在我的文档中加入评论功能"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:169
msgid ""
"Read the Docs doesn't have explicit support for this. That said, a tool like"
" `Disqus`_ (and the `sphinxcontrib-disqus`_ plugin) can be used for this "
"purpose on Read the Docs."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 没有对这一功能提供显式支持。不过，像 `Disqus`_ 这样的工具（以及 `sphinxcontrib-disqus`_ "
"插件）可以在 Read the Docs 上用于此目的。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:176
msgid "Can I remove advertising from my documentation?"
msgstr "我可以移除文档中的广告吗？"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:178
msgid ""
"Yes. See :ref:`Opting out of advertising <advertising/ethical-"
"advertising:Opting Out>`."
msgstr "可以。参见 :ref:`退出广告 <advertising/ethical-advertising:Opting Out>` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:182
msgid "How do I change my project slug (the URL your docs are served at)?"
msgstr "如何更改我的项目 slug（文档对外提供服务的 URL）？"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:184
msgid ""
"We don't support allowing folks to change the slug for their project. You "
"can update the name which is shown on the site, but not the actual URL that "
"documentation is served."
msgstr "我们不支持用户更改项目的 slug。你可以更新站点上显示的名称，但不能更改文档实际提供服务的 URL。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:188
msgid ""
"The main reason for this is that all existing URLs to the content will "
"break. You can delete and re-create the project with the proper name to get "
"a new slug, but you really shouldn't do this if you have existing inbound "
"links, as it `breaks the internet "
"<http://www.w3.org/Provider/Style/URI.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"主要原因在于，所有指向该内容的既有 URL 都会失效。你可以删除项目并用合适的名称重新创建以获得新 "
"slug，但如果已有外部链接指向你的文档，就真的不应这样做，因为这是在 `破坏互联网 "
"<http://www.w3.org/Provider/Style/URI.html>`_ 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:193
msgid ""
"Instead, you can consider *migrating your documentation to another domain* "
"with :doc:`/user-defined-redirects`."
msgstr "作为替代，你可以考虑借助 :doc:`/user-defined-redirects` *将文档迁移到另一个域名* 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:196
msgid ""
"If that isn't enough, you can request the change sending an email to "
"support@readthedocs.org."
msgstr "如果这样仍不满足需求，你可以发送邮件至 support@readthedocs.org 申请变更。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:200
msgid "Big projects"
msgstr "大型项目"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:203
msgid "How do I host multiple projects on one custom domain?"
msgstr "如何在一个自定义域名上托管多个项目？"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:205
msgid ""
"We support the concept of subprojects, which allows multiple projects to "
"share a single domain. If you add a subproject to a project, that "
"documentation will be served under the parent project's subdomain or custom "
"domain."
msgstr "我们支持子项目的概念，允许多个项目共享同一个域名。如果你为一个项目添加子项目，该子项目的文档将挂在父项目的子域名或自定义域名之下提供服务。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:209
msgid ""
"For example, Kombu is a subproject of Celery, so you can access it on the "
"`celery.readthedocs.io` domain:"
msgstr "例如，Kombu 是 Celery 的子项目，因此你可以在 `celery.readthedocs.io` 域名上访问它："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:213
msgid "https://celery.readthedocs.io/projects/kombu/en/latest/"
msgstr "https://celery.readthedocs.io/projects/kombu/en/latest/"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:215
msgid "This also works the same for custom domains:"
msgstr "对于自定义域名也是一样："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:217
msgid "http://docs.celeryq.dev/projects/kombu/en/latest/"
msgstr "http://docs.celeryq.dev/projects/kombu/en/latest/"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:219
msgid "You can add subprojects in the project admin dashboard."
msgstr "你可以在项目管理仪表盘中添加子项目。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:221
msgid ""
"For details on custom domains, see our documentation on :doc:`/custom-"
"domains`."
msgstr "关于自定义域名的详细信息，请参阅我们关于 :doc:`/custom-domains` 的文档。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:224
msgid "How do I support multiple languages of documentation?"
msgstr "如何支持多语言文档？"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:226
msgid ""
"Read the Docs supports multiple languages. See the section on "
":doc:`localization`."
msgstr "Read the Docs 支持多语言。参见 :doc:`localization` 一节。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:232
msgid "Sphinx"
msgstr "Sphinx"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:240
msgid "I want to use the Read the Docs theme"
msgstr "我想使用 Read the Docs 主题"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:242
msgid ""
"To use the Read the Docs theme, you have to specify that in your Sphinx's "
"``conf.py`` file."
msgstr "要使用 Read the Docs 主题，你需要在 Sphinx 的 ``conf.py`` 文件中指定它。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:245
msgid ""
"Read the `sphinx-rtd-theme documentation <https://sphinx-rtd-"
"theme.readthedocs.io/en/stable/installing.html>`_ for instructions to enable"
" it in your Sphinx project."
msgstr ""
"阅读 `sphinx-rtd-theme 文档 <https://sphinx-rtd-"
"theme.readthedocs.io/en/stable/installing.html>`_ ，了解在 Sphinx 项目中启用它的步骤。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:250
msgid "Image scaling doesn't work in my documentation"
msgstr "我的文档中图片缩放不生效"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:252
msgid ""
"Image scaling in ``docutils`` depends on ``Pillow``. If you notice that "
"image scaling is not working properly on your Sphinx project, you may need "
"to add ``Pillow`` to your requirements to fix this issue. Read more about "
":doc:`guides/reproducible-builds` to define your dependencies in a "
"``requirements.txt`` file."
msgstr ""
"``docutils`` 中的图片缩放依赖 ``Pillow`` 。如果你发现 Sphinx 项目中图片缩放不正常，可能需要在依赖中添加 "
"``Pillow`` 来修复该问题。阅读 :doc:`guides/reproducible-builds` 了解如何在 "
"``requirements.txt`` 文件中定义依赖。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:258
msgid "Python"
msgstr "Python"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:261
msgid "Can I document a Python package that is not at the root of my repository?"
msgstr "我可以为不在仓库根目录的 Python 包撰写文档吗？"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:263
msgid ""
"Yes. The most convenient way to access a Python package for example via "
"`Sphinx's autoapi`_ in your documentation is to use the "
"``python.install.method: pip`` (:ref:`config-file/v2:python.install`) "
"configuration key."
msgstr ""
"可以。要在文档中访问 Python 包（例如通过 `Sphinx's autoapi`_ ），最方便的方式是使用 "
"``python.install.method: pip`` （ :ref:`config-file/v2:python.install` ）配置键。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:267
msgid ""
"This configuration will tell Read the Docs to install your package in the "
"virtual environment used to build your documentation so your documentation "
"tool can access to it."
msgstr "这一配置会让 Read the Docs 把你的包安装到构建文档所用的虚拟环境中，这样你的文档工具就能访问它。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:274
msgid "Does Read the Docs work well with \"legible\" docstrings?"
msgstr "Read the Docs 能很好地处理“易读的”docstring 吗？"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/faq.rst:276
msgid ""
"Yes. One criticism of Sphinx is that its annotated docstrings are too dense "
"and difficult for humans to read. In response, many projects have adopted "
"customized docstring styles that are simultaneously informative and legible."
" The `NumPy <https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html"
"#docstring-standard>`__ and `Google "
"<https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-"
"docstrings>`__ styles are two popular docstring formats.  Fortunately, the "
"default Read the Docs theme handles both formats just fine, provided your "
"``conf.py`` specifies an appropriate Sphinx extension that knows how to "
"convert your customized docstrings.  Two such extensions are `numpydoc "
"<https://github.com/numpy/numpydoc>`_ and `napoleon <http://sphinxcontrib-"
"napoleon.readthedocs.io>`_. Only ``napoleon`` is able to handle both "
"docstring formats. Its default output more closely matches the format of "
"standard Sphinx annotations, and as a result, it tends to look a bit better "
"with the default theme."
msgstr ""
"可以。对 Sphinx 的一种批评是，其带注解的 docstring 过于稠密、人类难以阅读。为此，许多项目采用了自定义的 docstring "
"风格，使其兼具信息量与可读性。`NumPy <https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html"
"#docstring-standard>`__ 与 `Google "
"<https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-"
"docstrings>`__ 风格是两种流行的 docstring 格式。幸运的是，只要你的 ``conf.py`` 中指定了知道如何转换自定义 "
"docstring 的合适 Sphinx 扩展，默认的 Read the Docs 主题对这两种格式都能处理得很好。`numpydoc "
"<https://github.com/numpy/numpydoc>`_ 与 `napoleon <http://sphinxcontrib-"
"napoleon.readthedocs.io>`_ 就是两个这样的扩展。只有 ``napoleon`` 能同时处理两种 docstring "
